  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration found is config_025 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.724989 accuracy. All four aggregation×fusion combinations for scvi_n200+imagenet_vit_l are now tested, confirming transformer+weighted as optimal. scvi_n200 is clearly superior to pca_n2000 and scgpt, and imagenet_vit_l slightly edges resnet50. Question: config_028 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) completes the remaining untested cell in the scvi_n200+resnet50 aggregation×fusion matrix, testing whether avgpool+weighted with the cheaper image encoder could be competitive. Why this is the best last experiment: It uses the proven-best RNA encoder and the better fusion method (weighted), providing a final data point on the resnet50 variant. It is unlikely to surpass config_025 but completes the design space with the top RNA encoder. Expected cost is moderate (~4.5 GPU hours, comparable to config_017 at 4.82 h), keeping total budget around ~42.5 GPU hours. Since no remaining configuration is likely to beat 0.724989, this moderate-cost experiment minimizes additional GPU hours while still yielding useful confirmation of the architecture ranking."
